        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1950 BRDC International Trophy\n- People: Raymond Sommer, Peter Walker, Raymond Mays, Reg Parnell\n- Organizations: BRM\n- Products: BRM V16 cars\n- Places: Bourne, Lincolnshire, England\n- Roles: auto racing driver, entrepreneur\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1950 BRDC International Trophy, BRM entered two BRM V16 cars for Raymond Sommer, Peter Walker, Raymond Mays, and Reg Parnell.\n- Thomas Raymond Mays was born on 1 August 1899.\n- Thomas Raymond Mays was an auto racing driver and entrepreneur from Bourne, Lincolnshire, England.\n- Thomas Raymond Mays died on 6 January 1980.",
